WEBVTT

00:30:57.258 --> 00:31:00.183
Is there some level of discomfort
that's actually appropriate?

00:31:00.207 --> 00:31:01.524
SC: Oh, yeah. I mean, sure.

00:31:01.548 --> 00:31:03.734
I guess what I would say is,
well, two things.

00:31:03.758 --> 00:31:06.479
One is just to look at the data of it.

00:31:06.503 --> 00:31:08.354
This isn't only about,

00:31:08.378 --> 00:31:14.186
"Well, let's just make employees as happy
and comfortable at all times as possible."

00:31:14.210 --> 00:31:15.436
It's also about,

00:31:15.460 --> 00:31:18.865
"Well, how do you want people
to be most focused and most productive?"

00:31:18.889 --> 00:31:22.581
I really do believe in the serendipity
of people chatting with each other,

00:31:22.605 --> 00:31:24.425
so even in my ideal world,

00:31:24.449 --> 00:31:27.554
it would be designing office spaces
where there's plenty of spaces

00:31:27.578 --> 00:31:28.787
for people to do that.

00:31:28.811 --> 00:31:32.814
I'm just saying, you know, protect
the other side of human needs, as well.